From: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi mt76 dma npu tx path only for npu tx queues

mt76_dma_tx_queue_skb() sent every frame through mt76_npu_dma_add_buf()
as soon as an NPU was attached.  That is the TX of the MT7996/MT7992 NPU
firmware, whose TX queues carry MT_NPU_Q_TX.  The MT7916 one (Airoha
AN7552) does RX only and leaves the TX rings to the host: there the frames
were written in the NPU descriptor format into a plain WFDMA ring, the
card read garbage, its TX DMA stalled on the first frame and nothing,
not even a probe or an authentication response, went out.

Decide by the queue, as the rest of the NPU code does.

Signed-off-by: Lukasz M <lukasz1992m+openwrt@gmail.com>
---
--- a/dma.c
+++ b/dma.c
@@ -686,7 +686,7 @@ mt76_dma_tx_queue_skb(struct mt76_phy *p
 		goto free_skb;
 
 	/* TODO: Take into account unlinear skbs */
-	if (mt76_npu_device_active(dev) && skb_linearize(skb))
+	if (mt76_queue_is_npu_tx(q) && skb_linearize(skb))
 		goto free_skb;
 
 	t = mt76_get_txwi(dev);
@@ -738,7 +738,12 @@ mt76_dma_tx_queue_skb(struct mt76_phy *p
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto unmap;
 
-	if (mt76_npu_device_active(dev))
+	/*
+	 * Only a queue the NPU transmits from (MT7996/MT7992) takes the NPU
+	 * descriptor format.  The MT7916 NPU firmware does RX only: its TX
+	 * rings are the host's, in the plain WFDMA format.
+	 */
+	if (mt76_queue_is_npu_tx(q))
 		return mt76_npu_dma_add_buf(phy, q, skb, &tx_info.buf[1], txwi);
 
 	return mt76_dma_add_buf(dev, q, tx_info.buf, tx_info.nbuf,
